## Test Smell Audit — Academic Catalog (testsmells.org)

**Target:** `DataAccess.IntegrationTests/UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`  
**Framework:** MSTest 4.1 (.NET 10)  
**Integration calibration applied:** Class has `[TestCategory("Integration")]`

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 2           | 2              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Low      | 1           | 1              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic (Smell #1)

**Method:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 94)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Problem:** The `if/else` means one assertion path never executes per run. If `loaded` is never a `PremiumUser`, the discount-rate check is dead code.

**Fix:** Split into two explicit tests:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", 0.1m));
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com")!;
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Silent coverage gap — you'll never know which branch actually runs.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test / Unknown Test (Smell #4)

**Method:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)

```csharp
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
}
```

**Problem:** No assertion. Passes as long as no exception is thrown — but doesn't verify the data was actually persisted or is correct.

**Fix:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));

    var all = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, all.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — Insert could silently drop rows and this test still passes.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Sleepy Test (Smell #3)

**Method:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Problem:** Hard 3-second sleep. Non-deterministic (may be too short on slow CI, always too long locally). Adds 3 s to every suite run.

**Integration calibration:** Severity downgraded from High → Medium because async coordination waits are more acceptable in integration tests. Still a smell because a polling loop is strictly better.

**Fix:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var sent = await PollUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent, "Notification was not sent within timeout");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky failures in CI; needlessly slow suite.

---

#### 🟢 LOW — Assertion Roulette (Extended Smell)

**Method:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

Four assertions, zero failure messages. When one fails in CI, the stack trace shows a line number but no business context.

**Fix:** Add message parameters:

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Auto-generated Id should be positive");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower debugging when failures occur in CI logs.

---

### Smell-Free Patterns ✅

The remaining tests are well-structured:

- **`UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord`** — clear arrange/act/assert, focused scope.
- **`DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase`** — single concern, explicit null check.
- **`ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted`** — `Assert.AreEqual(3, ...)` is self-documenting (3 items just inserted; not a Magic Number).
- **`InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity`** — legitimate integration scenario with proper assertion.
- **General Fixture is clean** — both `_connection` and `_repository` are used by every test method.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, ...)` | 2 min |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | Split into 2 focused tests | 10 min |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with poll loop | 15 min |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | Add message strings to assertions | 5 min |

Fixes #1 and #2 eliminate false-confidence risks. Fix #3 removes flakiness. Fix #4 is polish for CI debuggability.
